"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the dogs"},{"surface":"இளைத்தன","parts":[{"text":"இளை","lemma":"iḷai","gloss":"to tire"},{"text":"த்த்","lemma":"tt","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"அன","lemma":"aṉa","gloss":"neuter plural suffix"}],"gloss":"are tired"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செல்லல்","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"cel","gloss":"go"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"al","gloss":"prohibitive suffix"}],"gloss":"do not go"},{"surface":"ஐஇய","parts":[{"text":"ஐஇய","lemma":"ஐஇய","gloss":"O Lord"}],"gloss":"O Lord","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உதுவெம்","parts":[{"text":"உது","lemma":"utu","gloss":"that nearby"},{"text":"எம்","lemma":"em","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"that our"},{"surface":"மூரே","parts":[{"text":"மூரே","lemma":"மூரே","gloss":"village indeed"}],"gloss":"village indeed","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓங்குவரை","parts":[{"text":"ஓங்கு","lemma":"ōṅku","gloss":"high"},{"text":"வரை","lemma":"varai","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"high mountain"},{"surface":"அடுக்கத்து","parts":[{"text":"அடுக்கத்து","lemma":"aṭukkam","gloss":"mountain slope (oblique)"}],"gloss":"of the mountain slope"},{"surface":"தீந்தேன்","parts":[{"text":"தீம்","lemma":"tīm","gloss":"sweet"},{"text":"தேன்","lemma":"tēṉ","gloss":"honey"}],"gloss":"sweet honey"},{"surface":"கிழித்த","parts":[{"text":"கிழி","lemma":"kiḻi","gloss":"to tear/break open"},{"text":"த்த்","lemma":"tt","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"torn/broken open"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குவையுடைப்","parts":[{"text":"குவையுடைப்","lemma":"குவையுடைப்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பசுங்கழை","parts":[{"text":"பசுங்கழை","lemma":"பசுங்கழை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தின்ற","parts":[{"text":"தின்ற","lemma":"தின்ற","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கயவாய்ப்","parts":[{"text":"கயவாய்ப்","lemma":"கயவாய்ப்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"பேதை","parts":[{"text":"பேதை","lemma":"pētai","gloss":"ignorant/young"}],"gloss":"ignorant/young"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yāṉai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"சுவைத்த","parts":[{"text":"சுவை","lemma":"cuvai","gloss":"to taste/chew"},{"text":"த்த்","lemma":"tt","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"chewed/tasted"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கூழை","parts":[{"text":"கூழை","lemma":"கூழை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மூங்கிற்","parts":[{"text":"மூங்கிற்","lemma":"மூங்கிற்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குவட்டிடை","parts":[{"text":"குவட்டிடை","lemma":"குவட்டிடை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யதுவே","parts":[{"text":"யதுவே","lemma":"யதுவே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"In the noisy forest, having chased the wild beasts, / the sun has set, and the dogs are tired. / Do not go, O Lord! That is our village, / on the high mountain slope, where sweet honey is torn open, / eating the green bamboo clumps, the large-mouthed, / young elephant chewed, / amidst the short bamboo peaks, it is there!","translation":"Having chased the wild beasts in the noisy forest, the sun has set, and your hunting dogs are tired. Do not go further, O Lord! Look there, that is our village, situated right amidst the short bamboo peaks, where the young, large-mouthed elephant chewed the green bamboo clumps after breaking open the sweet honeycombs on the high mountain slopes.","modern":"ஒலிக்கும் காட்டில் காட்டு விலங்குகளைத் துரத்தி வேட்டையாடியதால், பகல் பொழுதும் கழிந்தது; வேட்டை நாய்களும் இளைத்துவிட்டன. தலைவனே! இனிமேல் செல்லாதீர். அதோ தோன்றுவதுதான் எமது ஊர். உயர்ந்த மலைச்சரிவில் உள்ள இனிய தேன்கூடுகளைக் கிழித்துவிட்டு, திரண்ட பசுமையான மூங்கில்களைத் தின்ற, பெரிய வாயையுடைய இளமையான யானை சுவைத்த குட்டையான மூங்கில்கள் நிறைந்த மலை உச்சிக்கு நடுவே அது இருக்கிறது.","explanation":"The playmate (தோழி) is speaking to the hero (தலைவன்) who has come hunting in the mountain forest. She points out that the sun has set and his hunting dogs are exhausted. She invites him to stay at their village for the night, pointing to where it is located. The description of the elephant breaking open honeycombs and chewing the bamboo on the high slopes reflects the rich, fertile nature of the Kuriñci landscape. This imagery also subtly hints to the hero that he can easily find sweet union with the heroine in their hospitable village. Key words include 'ஞமலி' (hunting dog), 'கானத்து' (forest), 'எல்லின்று' (sun has set), and 'மூரே' (our village).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}